@startuml
title Agentic Delivery contexts, authority, and adapters
left to right direction
package "Domain contexts" {
  rectangle "Agentic Delivery Governance" as governance
  rectangle "Agentic Delivery Control Plane" as control
  rectangle "Agentic Primitives" as primitives
  rectangle "Developer Distribution" as distribution
}
rectangle "Architecture Authority\nCross-context authority, not a bounded context" as architecture
rectangle "Public .github repository adapter\nCommunity and template defaults" as public
rectangle "Private .github-private repository adapter\nMember profile and approved agent-publication boundary" as private
rectangle "GitHub native Issue Type definitions" as nativeTypes
rectangle "Organization issue-field definitions\nLifecycle Stage + Delivery State" as fieldDefinitions
rectangle "GitHub Projects fields\nSeparate planning projection" as projects
rectangle "GitHub App installation\nAccess + subscribed events" as app
rectangle "Repository Issues and pull requests" as work
rectangle "Per-issue field values API\nRepository-scoped values" as fieldValues
rectangle "Control Plane participant contract\nEnrollment + exact pins" as participants
rectangle "Consumer repositories" as consumers

architecture ..> governance : canonical organization decision text and architecture contract
architecture ..> control : pinned Architecture release
architecture ..> primitives : canonical ADR text and context references
architecture ..> distribution : canonical decision text and architecture contracts
app --> control : access and event delivery
participants --> control : separate enrollment check
control --> nativeTypes : reads issue type identity
control --> fieldDefinitions : reads field definitions and options
control --> fieldValues : reads/writes validated per-issue values
control --> work : origin-scoped issue and PR operations
governance ..> nativeTypes : issue classification semantics
governance ..> fieldDefinitions : lifecycle and delivery semantics
public --> work : forms and PR template defaults\n(binding unverified)
primitives --> private : reviewed, versioned projection target
primitives --> distribution : primitive-release.v1
control --> distribution : pinned workflow-bundle source
distribution --> consumers : versioned bootstrap and projection

note bottom
  Native Issue Type definitions and org issue-field definitions are separate
  organization settings; issue values use a distinct repository-scoped API.
  Projects fields are separate. The GitHub App grants access and delivers
  events; it does not distribute generic templates. Target integrations are
  not evidence of active pinning, entitlement, or end-to-end runtime behavior.
end note

@enduml
